      {
        "id": 55669,
        "name": "zerosatanmine",
        "username": "zerosatanmine",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/z/3be4f8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-19T20:17:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't get the impression there is any intention - or interest - in creating an alternate Mr. Fixer. Overdrive is good evidence to me they won't create an alternate. Also, the fact he's dead in the future (as implied by Golem Unity wearing his hat and the fact he's already in his 80s at the timing of Rook City) is good evidence he won't have a later version. He <em>could</em> have a younger version (as I'm sure he's had a great life history building to this point), but that probably would have shown up in Shattered Timelines if it was going to show up anyplace, so I'm willing to put good money on not getting an alternate Mr. Fixer.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Well, you can never say never for alternate character cards. I mean, they need ideas for future promos (I'm assuming they'll be promos in the future) and alternate character cards are an established promo so it could happen.</p>\n<p>Obviously Mr. Fixer's power would have to be named Strike if they were to make a promo card otherwise Overdrive would be useless. I didn't claim to be a game designer, I don't know how they'd make it work (I'll leave that in Christopher's capable hands) but you can't deny that it is at least a possibility.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:30:28.501Z",
