      {
        "id": 55677,
        "name": "Khedron",
        "username": "Khedron",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/khedron/{size}/1870_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-19T21:08:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"zerosatanmine\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/z/3be4f8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> zerosatanmine:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Well, you can never say never for alternate character cards. I mean, they need ideas for future promos (I'm assuming they'll be promos in the future) and alternate character cards are an established promo so it could happen.Obviously Mr. Fixer's power would have to be named Strike if they were to make a promo card otherwise Overdrive would be useless. I didn't claim to be a game designer, I don't know how they'd make it work (I'll leave that in Christopher's capable hands) but you can't deny that it is at least a possibility.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There are probably ways they could make a non-Strike power work. &nbsp;For example, something along the lines of \"Mr. Fixer deals 1 target 1 melee damage. &nbsp;Discard a card named 'Overdrive'; if you do, draw 3 cards.\"</p>",
        "post_number": 31,
        "post_type": 1,
